<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GoImmutability - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/goimmutability/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/goimmutability/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 148</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_148/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jan 2025 13:08:46 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_148/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Which of the following options is correct?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#10;&#10;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#10;&#10;func main() {&#10; str := &amp;#34;hello&amp;#34;&#10; str[0] = &amp;#39;x&amp;#39;&#10; fmt.Println(str)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. hello&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. xello&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;C&#10;&lt;a href="https://go.dev/play/p/WKuFSxIZZM8" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://golang.google.cn/ref/spec#String_types" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Go Official Documentation - String Types&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Strings are immutable: once created, it is impossible to change the contents of a string.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In the problem, &lt;code&gt;str&lt;/code&gt; is a string, and its content cannot be changed, so &lt;code&gt;str[0] = 'x'&lt;/code&gt; will cause an error.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 057</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_057/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:38 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_057/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Which of the following options is correct?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#10; str := &amp;#34;hello&amp;#34;&#10; str[0] = &amp;#39;x&amp;#39;&#10; fmt.Println(str)&#10;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A. hello&#10;B. xello&#10;C. compilation error&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Reference code and analysis: C.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Key takeaway: Strings in Go are read-only.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>